0353611"},{"store":"Octopart","url":"https://octopart.com/search?q=R7FA4E2B93CNH"}]}],"released":2023,"status":"active","datasheetUrl":"https://www.renesas.com/en/document/dst/ra4e2-group-datasheet","productUrl":"https://www.renesas.com/en/products/ra4e2","notes":["One CANFD channel (classic CAN and CAN-FD, ISO 11898-1). It needs an external transceiver.","USBFS is device-only (no host) and is missing on the 32-pin QFN. ROM boot mode supports SCI (UART), USB and SWD.","Only 2 SCI channels (SCI0, SCI9), each a UART, simple SPI or simple I2C. There is no classic IIC block: I2C is done by the single I3C module, which also talks to legacy I2C devices and is counted as i2c here. There are also 2 dedicated SPI.","Supply is 2.7-3.6 V only (no 5 V operation), though some pins are 5 V tolerant.","No capacitive touch, QSPI or crypto accelerator (TrustZone + TRNG only). There is 1 DAC channel and the 12-bit ADC has 12 inputs on 64-pin parts.","Deep Software Standby draws about 4.2 uA typ (about 16 uA when keeping 1 KB standby SRAM). Plain Software Standby is about 1.4 mA on this process. Active current is about 8.2 mA running CoreMark at 100 MHz.","The QFN-32 exposed pad is 3.2 x 3.2 mm, and KiCad has no exact match."],"sources":["https://www.renesas.com/en/document/dst/ra4e2-group-datasheet","https://www.renesas.com/en/products/ra4e2","https://www.renesas.com/en/products/ra4e2/part-details/r7fa4e2b93cfm-aa0","https://www.renesas.com/en/products/ra4e2/part-details/r7fa4e2b93cne-ba0","https://www.renesas.com/en/products/ra4e2/part-details/r7fa4e2b93cnh-ba0","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C20353608.html","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C20353610.html","https://www.lcsc.com/product-detail/C20353611.html","https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/tree/main/boards/renesas/ek_ra4e2"],"boards":["fpb-ra4e2"]}